From 1137f130378c0eaaae465f4e8c1ef3efc8afc581 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:14:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/35] Song change: countdown in loops, bars and beats; knobs
 on the playing song's master FX until it changes

While a loaded song is armed to start (LoadSongUI, UI_MODE_LOADING_SONG_UNESSENTIAL_SAMPLES_ARMED), the display
counts down to the change instead of 1.2.1's "Song will begin..." and "Loops remaining: N" popups:
- Session::getLaunchCountdown(): while repeats remain the loops remaining (numRepeatsTilLaunch, the current loop
  counting), in the last loop the bars remaining, in the last bar the beats (4-3-2-1 in 4/4), counted back from the
  launch event in swung ticks as getNumSixteenthNotesRemainingTilLaunch() does (so with swing and an external clock),
  each number shown for its whole bar or beat
- OLED: permanently on the title row (label, number in the title font), so the browser stays as it was with the song
  to come selected; 7-segment: the number, blinking while it counts loops as 1.2.1's repeats did, steady in the last
  loop. LoadSongUI::graphicsRoutine() redraws when what's shown changes, the launch event and the select encoder
  (repeats) at once; after the swap the title comes back
- OLED::removeWorkingAnimation() cleared one column past the image's right edge, i.e. the first pixel of the next
  row: a gap in the line under the title

From LOAD on while playing, the gold knobs and mod buttons are on the playing song's master FX (its GlobalEffectable
and params, as in the song view with affect entire, whatever that is set to; View::setActiveModControllableToSongFX()),
not whatever was selected (1.2.1 left e.g. a clip of the old song there), with the mod LEDs and knob indicators
showing its section and values (setKnobIndicatorLevels() works without a root UI while the knobs are on the playing
song). The mod knobs also act while LOAD is still held with the SD card busy, as they already did once armed. At the
swap (PlaybackHandler::doSongSwap()) the knobs are on nothing until the new song's view takes them, so nothing points
into the old song when it's deleted; knob turns held back in the encoders then are dropped, and a mod button's popup
held through the swap is taken down: the new song starts with its own values.

Tested in the emulator on this ELF (tests/songchange: OLED, 7-segment, swing, external clock, stop while armed): the
countdown right in every window, the swap at the launch event, the knobs on the old song's FX only.

